From 1b6458b8e43c850dc20e95d38e2f822be9cb828c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Apr 2026 19:34:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] =?UTF-8?q?fix:=20parts=20stock=20reconciliation=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20move=20deduction/restore=20to=20save=20time=20only?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bugs fixed:

1. Stock deducted immediately on AddPart (before ticket is saved)
   → AddPart() no longer touches stock at all. Deduction happens only
     when the ticket is actually committed to the DB.

2. RemovePart() never restored stock
   → RemovePart() no longer touches stock either. Restoration happens
     only on Save (diff) or Delete (full restore).

3. No diff on Save — saving an edited ticket didn't process part changes
   → SaveTicket() now calls ReconcileStock(snapshot, current) which diffs
     the two lists and applies only the delta: added parts are deducted,
     removed parts are restored. No double-deductions possible.

4. DeleteTicket() never restored parts
   → Before deleting, RestoreAllStock() is called with the ticket's
     full PartsUsed list so stock is fully returned.

5. Double-deduction possible (remove + re-add same part)
   → Eliminated because stock is never touched during editing.

Implementation:
- Added _savedPartsSnapshot: List<string> field — populated from DB
  in LoadFromTicket(), reset to empty in ClearForm() (new tickets).
- ReconcileStock(old, new): groups both lists by name (case-insensitive),
  computes per-part delta, calls ApplyStockDelta for each diff.
- RestoreAllStock(parts): used on delete — restores all parts grouped by qty.
